			PUNS & SHORT JOKES

By the time the final horse got his hay it was the last straw.

You shouldn't speed in the frozen north because the police will stop you =
cold.

The former minister bought a fabric store and became a man of the cloth.

Venus De Milo isn't all there=20

Two electricians were in a race that went down to the wire. (Pun of the =
Day)

			GROANERS & LONG JOKES

The other day, I went to the local dance club and showed the doorman my =
driver's license and one of the wheels off my car. He asked what the =
wheel was for. I said, "The guy on the radio said you were checking ID's =
and a tire."

A middle aged doctor was becoming burned out. One day he didn't go into =
the office but chose to stay on his farm. Most of the day, he sat on the =
edge of the well dropping pebbles into the water below. At mid =
afternoon, his nurse drove out to the farm to ask that he come to the =
office because they had so many patients there. He said, "I'll come =
soon, my dear.' About an hour later, when he had not come to the office, =
his nurse returned. As she drove up, he turned, fell into the well and =
drowned. The moral of this story is: Doctors should treat the sick and =
leave the well alone! (Gene Childs)

A guy woke up on the fifth of May at 5:55 am and took bus #55 to his =
work at a bank at 555 5th Avenue. When he opened his first task it was =
account number 55-555. The fifth person to walk into his office was his =
boss to tell him that he had a bonus of  $555 coming to him. He couldn't =
believe his luck. So he phoned his bookie to back horse number 5 in the =
fifth race. Guess what? The horse came in fifth.


